      "role": "user",
      "content": "oh right, my bad. here is the text from 4.2: 'During peak demand months (defined as Oct-Dec), the Supplier reserves the right to implement a price adjustment of up to 5% on the current base rate to account for market volatility, provided such adjustment is communicated via email.'\n\nso with that wording, is there a way for them to change the rates unexpectedly? i really need to know if this is going to mess with our budget stability during those months.",
